== T1 (reading i/iii, 'supermultiplicative subsets'): G(A) >= m_p(A)*m_q(A)?  m_k = min G over k-subsets
p=2 q=2 R=12: 132/495 sets violate; e.g. ((1, 3, 4, 5), 5, 3, 3)
p=2 q=3 R=13: 401/1716 sets violate; e.g. ((1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7), 7, 2, 4)
p=3 q=3 R=12: 21/220 sets violate; e.g. ((1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11), 11, 4, 4)
== T1b: weaker: does every n=pq-set with G(A)<=M contain a p-subset with G<=M/q or a q-subset with G<=M/p ?
